(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [13 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [14 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [15 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [17 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [23 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [24 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [25 1 "// or Repl."] [47 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [50 1 "// pyVersion315 is the version under REPR_PYTHON_VERSION=3.15 (queue 252): the pin 3.15.2, its Lib on sys.path."] [58 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [59 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [63 19 "// what w buffers (writeErr)"] [66 2 "// enc, errs: reconfigure()'s encoding and errors, \"\" the process's (stdioConfig); lineBuf its line_buffering"] [67 2 "// (queue 286: inspect's command line reconfigures sys.stdout's errors)"] [70 2 "// writeThrough: every write flushed, write_through (py-mods-1122: create_stdio's !buffered_stdio, -u or"] [71 2 "// PYTHONUNBUFFERED; libregrtest's --fast-ci adds -u when sys.stdout.write_through is false; reconfigure sets it)"] [75 1 "// stdioUnbuffered is the start's buffered_stdio negated (pylifecycle.c's create_stdio): -u (bin/pyi python's"] [76 1 "// PYI_UNBUFFERED, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is) or PYTHONUNBUFFERED (not under -E or -I)"] [91 1 "// writeErr is a failed write's or flush's OSError (py-eval-1122: with SIGPIPE ignored a closed pipe is EPIPE, a"] [92 1 "// BrokenPipeError, as CPython's BufferedWriter raises it). bufio keeps a write error for every later write and flush, so"] [93 1 "// the buffered bytes are dropped and the writer starts again on what it buffers: json.tool's handler dup2s /dev/null over"] [94 1 "// stdout and exits with EPIPE's status, which the shutdown's flush (status 120 when it fails) leaves."] [105 1 "// encoding is the stream's encoding: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [113 1 "// errors is the stream's errors handler: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [127 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [147 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [163 2 "// the standard streams' attributes (PY6b's request: doctest reads sys.stdout.encoding)"] [168 2 "// reconfigure (textio.c's _io_TextIOWrapper_reconfigure_impl; queue 286): encoding and errors (errors \"strict\" when"] [169 2 "// only the encoding is given), line_buffering (a line written flushes), write_through and newline checked; the"] [170 2 "// encoding looked up as the codec registry has it"] [286 4 "// a write error raises (queue 253: flush_std_files reports a failed flush at shutdown, status 120)"] [314 2 "// readlines(hint=-1) and iteration (py-design-1122: json.tool --json-lines reads sys.stdin.readlines()): IOBase's,"] [315 2 "// readline until the end, a positive hint stopping once the lines read hold that many characters"] [355 2 "// close (queue 249: multiprocessing's _close_stdin closes sys.stdin in a spawned child): the standard streams are"] [356 2 "// made with closefd=False (create_stdio), so the stream is flushed and marked closed, its descriptor left open"] [364 4 "// a failed flush raises after the close (TextIOWrapper.close: flush, then the buffer's close in a finally)"] [382 1 "// The standard streams' buffer (PY6e's REQUEST: subprocess's children write sys.stdout.buffer): a binary"] [383 1 "// view of the same bufio reader or writer, so text and bytes keep their order."] [485 1 "// exactArgsSelf checks a method's call: self and n arguments, no keywords."] [506 1 "// sysModule is the interpreter's sys module, made on first use."] [554 15 "// 3.15 (queue 252, PY315-SURVEY P7): the version the standard library (3.15.2's Lib) moves with"] [561 25 "// types.SimpleNamespace (PY6b: FrozenImporter makes them)"] [563 45 "// pyi's own .pyc files (PY6b): __pycache__/NAME.arbace-314.pyc, its own magic number"] [569 2 "// sys.flags as python3 -s -P -B runs (the references'): the struct sequence of sysmodule.c's flags_desc"] [582 47 "// -X int_max_str_digits, PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS (py-eval-1122)"] [585 2 "// -q, -E and -I (queue 296): config's quiet, use_environment and isolated (-I also -E's)"] [595 2 "// -i (queue 289): inspect and interactive; PYTHONINSPECT at start: inspect"] [602 2 "// -X utf8[=0|1] and PYTHONUTF8 (py-mods-1122: 3.14's too, pyi's default 1 kept; test_io's test_text_encoding runs"] [603 2 "// children with -X utf8=0 and -X utf8=1); -X warn_default_encoding and PYTHONWARNDEFAULTENCODING (config's"] [604 2 "// warn_default_encoding, PEP 597: _pyio's text_encoding warns; test_io's test_check_encoding_warning)"] [610 3 "// 3.15's lazy imports (queue 239): sys.flags.lazy_imports, sys.lazy_modules and the mode's and filter's API"] [623 18 "// -X options (queue 220: bin/pyi python passes them in PYI_XOPTIONS)"] [632 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, with CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [645 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): its call-family events (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [649 43 "// PY6c"] [652 2 "// pyi's own launcher when bin/pyi runs it (PY6e: tools/pyi/python3, CPython's command line), so that"] [653 2 "// script_helper and subprocess start pyi as CPython starts itself"] [674 3 "// PyErr_SetObject(PyExc_SystemExit, status): a tuple's items are the exception's arguments, None none"] [730 5 "// PyErr_GetExcInfo: the type, the exception, its __traceback__ (queue 223)"] [759 40 "// -1: -X cpu_count unset (os.process_cpu_count from sched_getaffinity)"] [803 2 "// breakpointhook (queue 304): sys_breakpointhook, $PYTHONBREAKPOINT's callable (pdb.set_trace when unset or empty, a"] [804 2 "// no-op for \"0\", a name without a dot builtins'), an unimportable one warned of and ignored; -E and -I ignore the"] [805 2 "// environment (Py_GETENV)"] [829 3 "// PyImport_Import: the leaf module (a non-empty fromlist)"] [847 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [853 4 "// _PyErr_Display: the traceback given put on an exception that has none (issue #18776)"] [861 4 "// traceback's display raises for a non-exception; the C fallback's print_exception line (queue 223)"] [870 2 "// is_remote_debug_enabled (queue 223): False, as a CPython built without Py_REMOTE_DEBUG answers (pyi has no"] [871 2 "// remote debugging, :remote-debugging); test_sys imports it at its top"] [932 3 "// dataclasses' slots=True (gh-135228): __dict__ and __weakref__ taken out of a heap type's dict"] [950 2 "// get_asyncgen_hooks and set_asyncgen_hooks (sysmodule.c; asyncio's event loops set theirs around run_forever):"] [951 2 "// the running thread's hooks, a sys.asyncgen_hooks; an argument left out keeps its hook, None clears it"] [985 2 "// _PySys_SetIntMaxStrDigits: 0 (no limit) or at least 640, sys.flags.int_max_str_digits with it (queue 202: a no-op,"] [986 2 "// so test_decimal's PyCoverage, which sets 7000, met the 4300 digits' limit)"] [1009 2 "// sys.getprofile and sys.setprofile: the legacy profiler over sys.monitoring (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [1016 2 "// sys.gettrace and sys.settrace: the legacy tracer over sys.monitoring (queue 219t, trace.go)"] [1043 2 "// threading.settrace_all_threads and setprofile_all_threads: every thread's trace or profile function"] [1086 24 "// its functions' __module__ \"sys\" (PY6f's REQUEST 8, as importBuiltin tags the others)"] [1090 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [1091 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [1112 1 "// sysAttr is sys.NAME when the sys module exists and has it, else nil."] [1120 1 "// sysModuleIfAny is the interpreter's sys module once made (interp->sysdict: sys.modules' entry is not needed, queue"] [1121 1 "// 253), else the one in sys.modules, else nil."] [1132 1 "// writeTo writes s to a file object: the interpreter's stdout when f is nil or None, a textFile directly,"] [1133 1 "// else f.write(s)."] [1153 1 "// exactArgsN checks a function's call: n positional arguments, no keywords (CPython's messages)."] [1167 1 "// cpythonSizeof is sys.getsizeof as CPython 3.14 answers it on a 64-bit build for the core immutable types"] [1168 1 "// and the list and tuple (the list's allocation taken as its length), 0 for any other object (PY6b's"] [1169 1 "// request: test_marshal sizes its big-memory tests by sys.getsizeof of an int at import). py-mods-1122: also a"] [1170 1 "// dict (dictSizeof), and in getsizeof a weak reference or proxy and a heap type's instance (objectSizeof:"] [1171 1 "// object.__sizeof__'s tp_basicsize, 16 and 8 a slot, with getsizeof's pre-header, the GC header and the managed"] [1172 1 "// __dict__ and __weakref__ pointers), so the pure OrderedDict's __sizeof__ (its __dict__, its map, its links and"] [1173 1 "// proxies) answers."] [1179 30 "// OrderedDict.__sizeof__ and the GC header"] [1193 36 "// sizeof(PyByteArrayObject) + ob_alloc"] [1218 1 "// objectSizeof is getsizeof's answer for a weak reference or proxy and a heap type's instance (sys.getsizeof's alone:"] [1219 1 "// tracemalloc's sizes are cpythonSizeof's), 0 for any other object."] [1223 18 "// sizeof(PyWeakReference), the GC header"] [1228 35 "// the built-in base's size (0: unknown here)"] [1233 12 "// Py_TPFLAGS_PREHEADER: the managed __dict__ and __weakref__ pointers"] [1235 17 "// the GC header (a heap type with a __dict__, a __weakref__ or slots is collected)"] [1240 1 "// dictSizeof is _PyDict_SizeOf with getsizeof's GC header: sizeof(PyDictObject) 48, the GC header 16, and a"] [1241 1 "// non-empty dict's keys object (PyDictKeysObject's 32 bytes, a byte of index a slot up to 256 slots, the usable"] [1242 1 "// two thirds of its slots as entries, 16 bytes each when every key is a str, else 24), its size the smallest power"] [1243 1 "// of two from 8 whose usable part holds the dict's entries."] [1273 1 "// versionInfoType is sys.version_info's struct sequence (PY6b's request: test_importlib reads its releaselevel):"] [1274 1 "// a tuple with the fields' names."] [1311 1 "// asyncgenHooks are each thread's async generator hooks (firstiter, finalizer; nil unset, None too), as the thread"] [1312 1 "// state's async_gen_firstiter and async_gen_finalizer: firstiter called on an async generator's first __anext__, asend,"] [1313 1 "// athrow or aclose (coro.go's asyncGenInitHooks; asyncio's tracking of unfinished async generators for"] [1314 1 "// shutdown_asyncgens); the finalizer kept, never called (pyi has no finalization, PY7)."] [1319 1 "// stdlibAdded315 and stdlibRemoved315 are 3.15.2's Python/stdlib_module_names.h against 3.14.10's (queue 252): its"] [1320 1 "// 296 names."] [1325 1 "// stdlibModuleNames is sys.stdlib_module_names (Python/stdlib_module_names.h of CPython 3.14.10, its 297 names; queue 223:"] [1326 1 "// traceback's \"Did you forget to import\" reads it)"] [1362 1 "// utf8Mode315 is 3.15's UTF-8 mode (PEP 686, Python/initconfig.c's config_init_utf8_mode; queue 237): on by default,"] [1363 1 "// -X utf8=0 (or PYTHONUTF8=0, which -E and -I ignore) turns it off, -X utf8 and -X utf8=1 on. 3.14's answer stays"] [1364 1 "// pyi's 1 (the locale's coercion pyi does not model)."] [1378 1 "// utf8ModeCheck315 is preconfig_init_utf8_mode's refusals (3.15; queue 237): -X utf8=V and PYTHONUTF8 other than 0 or 1"] [1379 1 "// are a fatal error at start, status 1"] [1402 1 "// startWarnOptions is sys.warnoptions as config_init_warnoptions orders it (queue 328), the lowest precedence first:"] [1403 1 "// \"default\" in development mode, PYTHONWARNINGS's comma-separated options (not under -E or -I), the command line's -W"] [1404 1 "// options (bin/pyi python's PYI_WARNOPTIONS, one a line, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_XOPTIONS"] [1405 1 "// is), then -b's \"default::BytesWarning\" or -bb's \"error::BytesWarning\"."] [1436 1 "// startBytesWarning is -b's count (bin/pyi python's PYI_BYTES_WARNING, read once and removed from the environment):"] [1437 1 "// sys.flags.bytes_warning."] [1459 1 "// init_interp_main: the warnings module imported at start when sys.warnoptions holds an option, so its"] [1460 1 "// _processoptions applies them (and reports an invalid one) before the main module runs (queue 328: test_warnings'"] [1461 1 "// test_warnings_bootstrap and test_improper_option)"] [1477 1 "// cpuCountConfig is PyConfig's cpu_count (py-eval-1122; Python/initconfig.c's config_init_cpu_count): -X cpu_count=N, else"] [1478 1 "// PYTHON_CPU_COUNT=N (not under -E or -I), N > 0; \"default\", unset or not a positive number: -1. os.cpu_count() answers it"] [1479 1 "// when set, and os.process_cpu_count() is then os.cpu_count() (os.py)."] [1500 1 "// intMaxStrDigitsConfig is PyConfig's int_max_str_digits (py-eval-1122; Python/initconfig.c's"] [1501 1 "// config_init_int_max_str_digits): -X int_max_str_digits=N, else PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS=N (not under -E or -I), N 0 (no"] [1502 1 "// limit) or at least 640; -1 when neither is given; for any other N (none, not a number, under 640) the start's error."] [1503 1 "// The start (an atStartHook) sets sys.set_int_max_str_digits' limit from it; sys.flags.int_max_str_digits shows it."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[210 13] [210 21] [229 57] [263 53] [